:1917,"tree_line_start":1916},{"depth":4,"role":"P","text":"","tree_line_end":1920,"tree_line_start":1918},{"depth":4,"role":"P","text":"","tree_line_end":1922,"tree_line_start":1921},{"depth":4,"role":"P","text":"","tree_line_end":1924,"tree_line_start":1923},{"depth":4,"role":"P","text":"","tree_line_end":1928,"tree_line_start":1925},{"depth":4,"role":"P","text":"","tree_line_end":1930,"tree_line_start":1929},{"depth":4,"role":"P","text":"","tree_line_end":1932,"tree_line_start":1931},{"depth":3,"role":"H3","text":"","tree_line_end":1935,"tree_line_start":1934},{"depth":3,"role":"P","text":"\n\n","tree_line_end":1941,"tree_line_start":1936},{"depth":3,"role":"P","text":"\n\n","tree_line_end":1947,"tree_line_start":1942},{"depth":3,"role":"P","text":"","tree_line_end":1950,"tree_line_start":1948},{"depth":4,"role":"H5","text":"","tree_line_end":1953,"tree_line_start":1952},{"depth":4,"role":"P","text":"","tree_line_end":1955,"tree_line_start":1954},{"depth":4,"role":"P","text":"","tree_line_end":1957,"tree_line_start":1956},{"depth":4,"role":"P","text":"","tree_line_end":1959,"tree_line_start":1958},{"depth":4,"role":"P","text":"","tree_line_end":1961,"tree_line_start":1960},{"depth":4,"role":"P","text":"","tree_line_end":1963,"tree_line_start":1962},{"depth":4,"role":"P","text":"","tree_line_end":1966,"tree_line_start":1964},{"depth":4,"role":"P","text":"","tree_line_end":1969,"tree_line_start":1967},{"depth":4,"role":"P","text":"","tree_line_end":1971,"tree_line_start":1970},{"depth":4,"role":"P","text":"","tree_line_end":1973,"tree_line_start":1972},{"depth":4,"role":"P","text":"","tree_line_end":1976,"tree_line_start":1974},{"depth":2,"role":"H2","text":"Appendix 1  ","tree_line_end":1983,"tree_line_start":1982},{"depth":3,"role":"H3","text":"Treatment of foreign state retirement pensions for the period 20.3.09 -12.4.10 ","tree_line_end":1990,"tree_line_start":1985},{"depth":3,"role":"P","text":"1 On 20.3.09 a Judge of the UT decided an appeal which affected how foreign state pensions were to be treated when considering entitlement to SPC\n1\n. Prior to the date of that decision, DMs should have treated a foreign state pension as not being part of a claimant’s retirement provision. The Judge decided that a foreign state pension may fall within the meaning of income from an overseas arrangement and therefore be part of the claimant’s retirement provision (see DMG 83066). Memo DMG 28/09 was issued in July 2009 to provide guidance on this to DMs. 1 SSWP v JK (PC) [2009] UKUT 55 (AAC) ","tree_line_end":2000,"tree_line_start":1991},{"depth":3,"role":"P","text":"2 From 13.4.10 SPC legislation was amended so that a foreign state retirement pension cannot be part of the claimant’s retirement provision and should be treated in the same way as a foreign social security benefit\n1\n. 1 SPC Regs, reg 15(2) ","tree_line_end":2010,"tree_line_start":2001},{"depth":4,"role":"H4","text":"Meaning of foreign state retirement pension ","tree_line_end":2014,"tree_line_start":2012},{"depth":4,"role":"P","text":"3 A foreign state retirement pension is\n1 ","tree_line_end":2020,"tree_line_start":2015},{"depth":4,"role":"L","text":"1. \nany pension paid under the law of a country outside the UK and \n2. \nin the nature of social security (similar to a RP paid under UK law). ","tree_line_end":2032,"tree_line_start":2021},{"depth":5,"role":"LI","text":"1. \nany pension paid under the law of a country outside the UK and ","tree_line_end":2027,"tree_line_start":2023},{"depth":5,"role":"LI","text":"2. \nin the nature of social security (similar to a RP paid under UK law). ","tree_line_end":2032,"tree_line_start":2028},{"depth":4,"role":"P","text":"1 reg 1(2) ","tree_line_end":2035,"tree_line_start":2033},{"depth":4,"role":"P","text":"4 From 13.4.10 where the claimant is in receipt of a foreign state retirement pension then that income should be taken into account in the same way as any other income which is not part of the claimant’s retirement provision. It does not form part of the claimant’s retirement provision and so the treatment of it is unaffected by any AIP\n1\n. 1 SPC Act 02, s 7(6); SPC Regs, reg 11(2) ","tree_line_end":2046,"tree_line_start":2036},{"depth":5,"role":"H5","text":"Example ","tree_line_end":2049,"tree_line_start":2048},{"depth":5,"role":"P","text":"Juan is in receipt of SPC and the DM has set an AIP. On 30.4.10 Juan receives the first payment of a state retirement pension paid by the Spanish government. The DM ","tree_line_end":2052,"tree_line_start":2050},{"depth":5,"role":"P","text":"decides that the income does not form part of Juan’s retirement provision because it ","tree_line_end":2054,"tree_line_start":2053},{"depth":5,"role":"P","text":"is income from a foreign state retirement pension. This means that the rules whereby a claimant’s retirement provision is fixed for the duration of the AIP do not apply to this income. The DM takes the income into account when it is paid because ","tree_line_end":2058,"tree_line_start":2055},{"depth":5,"role":"P","text":"it is not part of the claimant’s retirement provision. ","tree_line_end":2060,"tree_line_start":2059},{"depth":4,"role":"H4","text":"Supersession ","tree_line_end":2063,"tree_line_start":2062},{"depth":4,"role":"P","text":"A change in the law is a relevant change of circumstances (see DMG 04109)\n1\n. From ","tree_line_end":2070,"tree_line_start":2064},{"depth":4,"role":"P","text":"13.4.10\n DMs should be considering superseding awards of SPC where the claimant is in receipt of a foreign state retirement pension. The DM should supersede the award of SPC where the foreign state retirement pension has been treated as part of the claimant’s retirement provision and that supersession results in a change in the amount of SPC which the claimant is entitled to. The date of change for the purposes of the supersession will be 13.4.10\n2\n. ","tree_line_end":2077,"tree_line_start":2071},{"depth":4,"role":"P","text":"1 SS CS (D&A) Regs, reg 6(2)(a); 2 reg 7(30) ","tree_line_end":2080,"tree_line_start":2078},{"depth":5,"role":"H5","text":"Example ","tree_line_end":2083,"tree_line_start":2082},{"depth":5,"role":"P","text":"Camilla is in receipt of SPC. The DM set an AIP on 6.5.08 for a period of five years. On 1.5.09 Camilla began to receive a state retirement pension from the Italian ","tree_line_end":2087,"tree_line_start":2084},{"depth":5,"role":"P","text":"government. The DM determined that the pension formed part of Camilla’s ","tree_line_end":2090,"tree_line_start":2088},{"depth":5,"role":"P","text":"retirement provision on the grounds that it was an income from an overseas arrangement. Since there was an AIP already in place on 1.5.09 the foreign state retirement pension could have no affect on the amount of SPC that Camilla was entitled to. ","tree_line_end":2092,"tree_line_start":2091},{"depth":5,"role":"P","text":"From 13.4.10 the DM determines that due to a change in the law, Camilla’s Italian pension no longer falls to be treated as part of her retirement provision. The DM takes the payment of that foreign state retirement pension into account as income. The AIP which was set for a period of five years remains in place because none of the circumstances which may bring it to an end have occurred (see DMG 83030 and 83050). ","tree_line_end":2095,"tree_line_start":2093},{"depth":2,"role":"H2","text":"Appendix 2 ","tree_line_end":2099,"tree_line_start":2097},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Period in which the AIP was originally Date on which AIP will now end determined to end 1 April 2019 to 14 April 2019 14 July 2016 15 April 2019 to 30 April 2019 28 July 2016 1 May 2019 to14 May 2019 14 August 2016 15 May 2019 to 30 May 2019 28 August 2016 1 June 2019 to 14 June 2019 14 October 2016 15 June 2019 to 30 June 2019 28 October 2016 1 July 2019 to 14 July 2019 14 November 2016 15 July 2019 to 31 July 2019 28 November 2016 1 August 2019 to 14 August 2019 14 December 2016 15 August 2019 to 31 August 2019 28 December 2016 1 September 2019 to 14 September 2019 14 February 2017 15 September 2019 to 30  September 2019 28 February 2017 1 October 2019 to 14 October 2019 14 March 2017 15 October 2019 to 31 October 2019 28 March 2017 1 November 2019 to 14 November 2019 14 April 2017 15 November 2019 to 30 November 2019 28 April 2017 1 December2019 to 14 December 2019 14 June 2017 15 December 2019 to 31 December 2019 28 June 2017 1 January 2020 to 14 January 2020 14 July 2017 15 January 2020 to 31 January 2020 28 July 2017 1 February 2020 to 14 February 2020 14 September 2017 \n15 February 2020 to 29 February 2020 1 March 2020 to 14 March 2020 15 March 2020 to 31 March 2020 1 April 2020 to14 April 2020 15 April 2020 to 30 April 2020 1 May 2020 to 14 May 2020 15 May 2020 to 31 May 2020 1 June 2020  to 14 June 2020 15 June 2020 to 30 June 2020 1 July 2020 to 14 July 2020 15 July 2020 to 31 July 2020 1 August 2020 to 14 August 2020 15 August 2020 to 31 August 2020 1 September 2020 to 14 September 2020 15 September 2020 to 30 September 2020 1 October2020 to 14 October 2020 15 October 2020 to 31 October 2020 1 November 2020 to 14 November 2020 15 November 2020 to 30 November 2020 1 December 2020 to 14 December 2020 15 December 2020 to 31 December 2020 1 January 2021 to 14 January 2021 15 January 2021 to 31 January 2021 1 February 2021 to 14 February 2021 15 February 2021 to 28 February 2021 \n28 September 2017 14 October 2017 28 October 2017 14 December 2017 28 December 2017 14 January 2018 28 January 2018 14 March 2018 28 March 2918 14 April 2018 28 April 2018 14 June 2018 28 June 2018 14 July 2018 28 July 2018 14 August 2018 28 August 2018 14 October 2018 28 October 2018 14 November 2018 28 November 2018 14 January 2019 28 January 2019 14 February 2019 28 February 2019 ","tree_line_end":2107,"tree_line_start":2100},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 March 2021 to 14 March 2021 14 March 2019 15 March 2021 to 5 April 2021 28 March 2019” ","tree_line_end":2111,"tree_line_start":2108},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"The content of the examples in this document (including use of imagery) is for illustrative purposes only ","tree_line_end":2114,"tree_line_start":2112}],"bounds":{"stderr_bytes":65536,"stdout_bytes":16777216,"timeout_seconds":45},"command":["/opt/homebrew/bin/pdfinfo","-struct-text","source/pdf/dmg-vol14-ch83.pdf"],"diagnostics":{"roles_not_emitted":{"Caption":1,"Figure":4,"LBody":80,"Lbl":81,"Link":26,"NonStruct":34,"Note":10,"Part":1,"Reference":70,"Sect":63,"Span":94,"TOC":1,"TOCI":36},"text_joiner":"\n","tree_lines":2118,"unparsed_line_count":28,"unparsed_line_samples":[{"text":"            Object 430 0","tree_line":565},{"text":"            Object 421 0","tree_line":568},{"text":"            Object 424 0","tree_line":571},{"text":"            Object 410 0","tree_line":572},{"text":"            Object 417 0","tree_line":579},{"text":"            Object 425 0","tree_line":582},{"text":"            Object 418 0","tree_line":585},{"text":"            Object 412 0","tree_line":586},{"text":"            Object 438 0","tree_line":708},{"text":"          Object 443 0","tree_line":825},{"text":"          Object 446 0","tree_line":840},{"text":"          Object 453 0","tree_line":845},{"text":"          Object 462 0","tree_line":852},{"text":"          Object 450 0","tree_line":855},{"text":"          Object 456 0","tree_line":860},{"text":"          Object 454 0","tree_line":866},{"text":"          Object 475 0","tree_line":886},{"text":"          Object 467 0","tree_line":889},{"text":"          Object 474 0","tree_line":894},{"text":"          Object 466 0","tree_line":897}],"unparsed_line_samples_omitted":8},"document_id":"dmg-vol14-ch83","document_key":"dmg:dmg-vol14-ch83","family":"dmg","frozen_tagged_flag":"yes","limitations":["PDF-declared roles are source structure, not proof of correct reading order, accessibility, coherent legal units or applicability.","Text in a retained block joins its descendant quoted tree fragments with a